title: View Window(s)
manual:

The view draws the current system in 3D: atoms, bonds, cell and the objects added to the
scene. The main view follows the system selected in the tree; the combo at
the right end of the toolbar also chooses the system shown.

# Toolbar

- "An" (D) shows the annotation toolbar, with the tools that draw shapes, text,
  measurements and axes.
- "Atoms" (1), "Bonds" (2), "Labels" (3), "Cell" (4) and "Poly" (5)
  show or hide those objects.
- "Cells" shows the number of unit cells drawn along a, b and c (Keypad + and - change
  it); its popup sets them. "k-space" (Ctrl+K) switches to the reciprocal-space scene.
- "Camera": "Orthographic" or "Perspective" projection, buttons that align the camera
  with the cell or Cartesian axes (A, B, C, X, Y, Z), the "Reset distance" ratio, the
  "Camera lock" between systems (main view only) and the background "Color".
- "All" applies the settings of this scene to the systems selected in the tree;
  "Reset" returns the scene to its defaults.
- "Show" opens the Display Settings window, which selects the part of the system drawn;
  "Draw" adds an object: a whole style, the atoms, bonds, labels and polyhedra, and the
  rest in the "Cell and Symmetry", "Fields", "Annotations" and "Guides" submenus;
  "Objects" lists the objects.
- "Tools" is the Tools menu for this system; "View" opens a new view of the same scene.

# Mouse and view modes

The combo at the bottom sets the view mode; its tooltip lists the bindings.

- "Navigate": drag with the left button to rotate, the middle button to spin and the
  right button to pan; the wheel zooms and a right double-click resets the view.
  Double-click atoms to select them for a measurement (distance, angle, dihedral) and
  right-click to add or remove it.
- "Select" (or hold Shift in Navigate): click or drag a rectangle to select atoms,
  right-click to select a molecule.
- "Move Molecules" (hold Ctrl) drags a molecule as a rigid body; "Move Atoms"
  (Ctrl+Shift) drags one atom.
- The pick, builder, "Interact (MD)" and "Edit Object" modes are set by the window that
  needs them and return to Navigate when done. Escape exits the mode and clears the
  selection.

# Several views

Windows > New View Window, or the "View" button, opens an alternate view. Tool
windows anchor to the view they were opened from and follow the system it shows.
File > Export to Image... (Ctrl+Shift+E) writes the view to a PNG file.
